From 9a739332491d4bc8214072acd8675430761c2af2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:05:15 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 44/44] GE: a texture over two render targets reads the one
 that drew there

A render target is taken as 272 rows of its row length, so a short buffer
(256x128) takes in the buffer drawn right after it in VRAM. A texture whose
first texel lay in both was read from the target drawn last, even where that
target never drew: a texture over a copy of the previous frame read the
undrawn rows of this frame's copy just below it. The GE reads whatever was
last written at the address.

Among the targets that take in the first texel, one whose drawn rectangle
(the scissors of its draws, as palette views use) holds it now wins; among
equals the newest, as before. <prefix>_NO_TARGET_DRAWN_AREA restores the
old choice; <prefix>_TRACE_FB_TEXTURES logs where the two differ, and the
census counts fbtex.target_by_drawn_area (info) or, with the switch,
fbtex.undrawn_rows_of_newer_target.

Seen in Dissidia 012: Lightning's Water refracts a half-size copy of the
last frame at 0x041A6000, right after this frame's copy at 0x04196000; it
came out as a dark negative and is now a clear sphere, at 1x and 4x, 30 and
60 fps. Not verified on a handheld.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
